# 7. PHASE FOUR — TRUE 3D RELATIONSHIP EXPLORER

This is one of the most important differentiating features.

The current Relationship Explorer already has an SVG relationship diagram and an optional 3D preview.

Enhance it into a genuine spatial learning environment.

## 7.1 Full 3D relationships

Every relationship node with a valid geometry mapping should be available in the 3D experience.

The objective is not to duplicate structures or create an independent model for each node.

Reuse the central anatomical atlas and existing Three.js rendering infrastructure.

When a student selects a central structure:

1. Identify its verified incoming and outgoing relationships.
2. Determine which associated structures have individual mesh mappings.
3. Highlight the structures using their relationship roles.
4. Draw directional connections between them.
5. Display their correct anatomical names.
6. Explain why they are connected.
7. Allow the student to select any connected structure.
8. Update the information panel and network accordingly.

## 7.2 Relationship visualization categories

Support different relationship types, including:

- Origin
- Insertion
- Articulation
- Attachment
- Innervation
- Arterial supply
- Venous drainage
- Lymphatic drainage
- Antagonist
- Part of
- Has part
- Adjacent to
- Supports

Provide a distinctive, accessible visual treatment for each relationship type.

Do not use a relationship colour alone to convey meaning. Show explicit labels and a legend.

## 7.3 Spatial accuracy

A connection must be drawn in anatomically appropriate locations.

Use:

- Verified attachment points when available.
- Mesh surface coordinates when reliable.
- Structure centres or bounds only when an exact attachment point is unavailable.
- Directional arrows where direction has anatomical meaning.

Do not draw anatomically precise-looking connections from arbitrary coordinates.

For concept-only structures:

- Show their information.
- Show their relationship description.
- Explicitly explain that an individual 3D structure is unavailable.
- Do not fabricate its geometry.

## 7.4 Relationship interface

